WP19 no-claim proof:

- Inventory is not usage: compile requests require explicit proof kinds and do
  not turn inventory-only rows into runtime decisions.
- Running is not foreground: no foreground inference is introduced.
- Foreground is not content: no screen, title, chat, or content fields are
  introduced.
- AI cannot enforce: compile requests accept typed evidence/proof refs, not raw
  model text or unvalidated AI output.
- Category/risk/multiplayer/UGC/purchase target labels cannot enforce by
  themselves; compiled output must cite evidence and capability refs.
- Manual-required cannot call adapters: unproved block-launch compiles to
  manual-required with disabled handoff.
- Wrong device, wrong local user, and stale evidence are rejected before
  compile output is accepted.
